# PAD-530: the surface's own seek, length and position, at LE 1.06's distances from surface_play, each the same code
# (seek calls the player's gst_element_seek, length and position its query_duration / query_position). A mode's clip
# the game's own clip took the surface from comes back where it would be by then, once the game's clip is over: when
# the game asks for its main-play video (MainPlayLoop_<film>, as on LE), or the surface is idle. Seen in the emulator
# 2026-10-11 (stock card, hidden, muted) as on LE: the game's own Ball Lock (effect 117) and Extra Ball (effect 279,
# award_screen(279, 0, 0, 0x7a7e00) as Pro 0x5e8ec) over a mode file's 111.9 s clip - back at 8785 ms and 15372 ms.
site surface_seek     0x00574d5c 0xe92d43f0 0xe1a07003
site surface_duration 0x00574a14 0xe5d030d4 0xe92d40f0
site surface_position 0x00574bb8 0xe5d030d4 0xe92d40f0
# PAD-725: the game's reel (a clip of its own kept in step with a song): its tick waits while a clip of
# ours has the bank's surface. Found by what it calls (surface_position, surface_seek, surface_play) and
# its prologue (push; mov r4, r0; ldr r0, [r0, #0x1c]; cmp r0, #0; popeq).
site reel_tick       0x0044fe00 0xe92d47f0 0xe1a04000
text backdrop_idle MainPlayLoop
# PAD-722: the backdrop on the bank's surface, as on LE 1.06 (PAD-521): a mode's loop is played there again whenever
# it is idle. Seen on the glass in the emulator 2026-10-25 (stock card, hidden, muted): a blocks mode's own loop in the
# TV frame, taken back each time the game asked for MainPlayLoop_DrNo.
value backdrop_surface 1
# PAD-722: the game's own status bar under the TV (scene hud 7de1c159, the LE's): the score display's getter, LE
# 1.06's 0x1862dc on this build (the LE recipe places it strictly; the same 0x128-byte singleton). Its frame update
# 0x185ac4 reads the LE's fields: the nodes at +0x104/+0x108/+0x10c/+0x114, the wipe's frame +0x11c, the four flags
# +0x11e..+0x121 - the runtime's defaults. Seen on the glass in the emulator 2026-10-25: a blue bar named FRWL WIZARD,
# its clock draining along it, held again when a display of the game's moved it.
site status_bar       0x00184aec 0xe92d4038 0xe3004138
