# PAD-621: the right return up post, as the game's own mini-wizards hold the ball with it through their start
# clip when the Right ramp starts them (BottomLaneUpPost, device 9; the game's own command 255 for 64 ms, then
# AD_BOTTOM_LANE_UP_POST_POWER - adjustment 178 - for 20 s; its v[3] reads AD_BOTTOM_LANE_UP_POST_DISABLED).
# A Device-framework object: its update OFFs it on most switch hits and its tick raises it 1875 ticks on a pending
# raise, unless a process controls it (+0x10). So a hold takes it (the framework's take / give), and clears its
# countdown (+0x20) and pending raise (+0x24) before giving it back, so the give's update lowers it.
text right_return_up_label Right return up post
text right_return_up_drive 8 7 255 64 a178
data right_return_up_obj   0x0081acf0
